r4dx third-party notices
========================

libr4d
------
r4dx builds against the HIP kernel library libr4d (RDNA4 / gfx1201 attention, Gated DeltaNet and GEMM
kernels), written by StillDeadcode and contributors:

    https://codeberg.org/StillDeadcode/libr4d

The upstream repository does not state a licence. The kernels are used in r4dx for experimentation and
all credit for them belongs to their authors. If an author would like them removed, or would like different
attribution, please open an issue and they will be changed or removed promptly.

Additions and changes made in this repository on top of libr4d (for example the trellis GEMM kernels, the
exact-wide and split-KV prefill attention launches and the M=256 GEMM prototype) are part of r4dx and covered
by its MIT licence. That licence does not extend to the unmodified upstream code.

